<article class="env-lemma" id="074V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/074V">Lemma <span data-tag="074V">11.7.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a finite central simple algebra over $k$. If $K \subset A$ is a subfield, then the following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$[A : k] = [K : k]^2$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$K$ is its own centralizer, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$K$ is a maximal commutative subring. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Theorem <a href="/tag/074T" data-tag="074T">11.7.1</a> shows that (1) and (2) are equivalent. It is clear that (3) and (2) are equivalent. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>